[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017729533","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117190#issuecomment-4017729533","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117190","id":4017729533,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vea_9","user":{"login":"Jesusemora","id":32273722,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMjczNzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32273722?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora","html_url":"https://github.com/Jesusemora","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jesusemora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-08T00:20:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-08T00:20:42Z","body":"I think it's very simple, the `transforms` of the children of CSG are used to perform boolean operations.\nI don't see a reason why someone would want to scale a CSG node without affecting children (since changing `size` already doesn't affect children).\n\nScaling a parent without affecting children would mean that the children are being scaled to maintain their shape.\nIf the parent is scaled to 2.0, the children will have to be scaled by 0.5. And, in this case, if the parent is scaled by 0.5, the children will scale by 2.0.\nI don't have time to download the latest version, **the test doesn't have the altered Nodes** . Please check the scale of the parent and children to see if this is the case.\n\nThe solution would be to take into account scale of CSG node during autosmooth step and somehow fix this. This would be an step that has to be applied to every vertex, and it could have a performance cost.\n\nI would try this: (line 623)\n```C++\nTransform3D trans = get_transform();\nPlane p(trans.xform(n->faces[i].vertices[0]), trans.xform(n->faces[i].vertices[1]), trans.xform(n->faces[i].vertices[2]));\n```\nIs it worth it? how many people scales CSGs?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017729533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4048431831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117190#issuecomment-4048431831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117190","id":4048431831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7xTirX","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-12T17:00:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-12T17:00:41Z","body":"People non-uniformly scale rectangular prisms (boxes) and spheres a lot more in csg than regular assets for level prototyping.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4048431831/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]